	j > i / _(s)#
	ð > ∅ / _#
	ð > t / _s#
	β > u / V_(s)#
	β > {∅,f} / C_(s)# (the latter is rare)
	n > ∅ / V_# (did not occur in extreme western areas, some northern areas, the southeast,
				and the east)
	n > ∅ / _s# (except for eastern and southeastern dialects)
	n > ∅ / r_(s)#?
	k:[+ long] > t͡ʃ / _a (in the east and northeast)
	l:[+ long] > l (in the south)
	# r:[+ long]~r stuff—not sure what was going on here, but it seems like this
	# 			distinction lingered on into the literary period, but the two may have been in the
